# Plan → Build workflow

## Modes

**Plan mode:** Produce or update a plan only. No file edits. Product questions happen here.

**Build mode:** Execute the approved plan file completely. Full auto — no clarifying questions unless blocked (missing `.env`, migration push failed twice, destructive action).

## Saved project defaults

- **Auth:** Login once at hub entry ([`HubAuthGate`](src/components/HubAuthGate.tsx)); all rooms unlocked after sign-in.
- **Data:** No mock DB rows. UI may show a labeled demo empty state until the user adds the first real item; then demo hides permanently.
- **Supabase:** Real queries only after schema exists. Run `npm run db:push` when CLI is linked; otherwise in-app Setup panel with copy-paste SQL.
- **Design:** Cleanroom Light Glassmorphism — match [`EerdmansHub`](src/EerdmansHub.tsx).

## Build checklist (agent)

1. Implement all plan todos without re-asking access questions (see [`PROJECT_SETUP.md`](PROJECT_SETUP.md)).
2. Add/update migrations in `supabase/migrations/`.
3. Run `npm run db:push` if `supabase/.temp/project-ref` exists.
4. Run `npm run build` and fix errors before finishing.

## Do not re-ask

- Supabase vs localStorage (Supabase)
- Per-room auth (hub gate only)
- Build autonomy (full auto)
